# Paths excluded from Semgrep (frappe/semgrep-rules, run by
# .github/workflows/linter.yml and the local pre-commit hook).
#

# rules/security/authorization.yml:relaxed-permissions matches any DocPerm
# object naming the "All" role, with no way to express that the grant is
# scoped. DocType JSON has no comment syntax, so there is nowhere to put a
# `nosemgrep` annotation — the file is the only granularity available.
#
# The four DocTypes below are per-user chat records, so every user needs a
# grant and "All" is the only role every user holds. The grant is narrowed
# three ways:
#
#   1. `if_owner: 1` on the All DocPerm, so the role reaches only rows the
#      user created. Frappe exempts `create` from if_owner, and each row is
#      written with `user = frappe.session.user`, so owner and user always
#      agree (see chat/doctype/fac_chat_message/fac_chat_message.py).
#   2. `permission_query_conditions` hooks that filter every list query to
#      `user = <session user>` (chat/utils/permissions.py).
#   3. `has_permission` hooks that repeat the check per document.
#
# Each DocType also carries a separate System Manager DocPerm without
# if_owner, so administrators are unaffected.
#
# Removing a file from this list is the right move the moment its "All"
# grant stops being owner-scoped.

frappe_assistant_core/chat/doctype/fac_chat_message/fac_chat_message.json
frappe_assistant_core/chat/doctype/fac_chat_usage_log/fac_chat_usage_log.json
frappe_assistant_core/chat/doctype/fac_chat_user_preferences/fac_chat_user_preferences.json
frappe_assistant_core/chat/doctype/fac_chat_banner_dismissal/fac_chat_banner_dismissal.json
